WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.400
&gt;&gt; Malcolm Grant: So may we move quickly on
to the report of the Chief Executive.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.180
&gt;&gt; Simon Stevens: Thanks, Malcolm.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:18.170
I will just draw out a few items from my written
report.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.940
I think that much of the substance is going
to be covered elsewhere on the agenda.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:29.650
First, I want to thank all of our team who
very successfully put together the NHS Expo

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.830
in Manchester earlier this month.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:39.120
It was a really fantastic event, I think,
despite all of the pressures and trials and

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.110
tribulations around the frontline of the Health
Service.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.960
There was a sense, on the part of the people
who were there, that actually there is a route

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.219
forward that a number of people can chart
and are getting on with, and it was a very

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:56.470
practical, sleeves rolled up kind of event,
at no cost to the NHS or to taxpayers.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:02.859
Secondly, we have previously talked about
the creation of the new NHS success regimes

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:08.490
in struggling parts of the country, that we
launched at the NHS Confederation conference

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.880
in the summer.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:18.110
They are now up and running, and I and Mike
Richards and colleagues from TDA and Monitor

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.930
will be up in Cumbria in a few days' time.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:28.860
The team to lead the work in northeast and
west Devon and in south Essex is also being

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.250
put in place.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:36.130
The proposition here is that by coming together
between NHS England, NHS Improvement, CQC

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.890
and others, working with local leaders, we
aim to cut through some of the Gordian knots

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.460
that have stood in the way of putting these
parts of the country onto a sustainable footing.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.800
We will see, but it feels like the right approach.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:59.289
Third, tomorrow we will be announcing the
results of the acute care vanguards referenced

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:02.100
in my Board report.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:09.360
I will hold fire until then, other than to
say that we had 65 expressions of interest

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:18.230
and, as described in my report, a very good
two-day peer event at the Oval to identify

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.530
what these new types of hospital partnership
and collaboration should be.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:30.890
Fourth, Paul will talk about the position
for the current year, 2015/16 - particularly

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.750
finances - and Barbara about NHS performance.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:42.940
I would simply underline that I think there
is now a wide understanding that, absent decisive

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:49.540
action on temporary staffing in the next several
weeks, it will be very hard for the NHS overall

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:56.570
to deliver its side of the funding bargain
for 2015/16.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:02.200
We have no choice now but to act, and the
clear expectation is that, collectively, we

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.640
will do so.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.320
More on that will follow.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.770
As far as 2016/17 is concerned, we are obviously
in the early stages of the spending review

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.970
process with the Treasury.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:20.319
We will need to await the outcome of that
on 25th November before we are able to set

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:29.140
allocations, tariffs or other elements of
the ask for the Health Service for next year.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.980
In the meantime, however, together with NHS
Improvement we intend to communicate some

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.640
of the broad parameters within which we should
be thinking about next year, and also to set

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.290
in train a more fundamental process for local
health communities to begin to think about

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:49.470
how their care systems need to be transformed
between now and 2020, in line with the five-year

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.160
forward view.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:59.220
I and the new Chief Executive of NHS Improvement,
with colleagues, will be holding face-to-face

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:06.680
meetings with all of the chief execs from
across the NHS - one in Leeds, one in London

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:12.500
- in the first part of December to kick off
the results of the spending review and the

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:19.519
new shared processes which NHS Improvement
and NHS England will be moving forward with.

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:21.049
Let me stop there for now.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:22.920
&gt;&gt;Malcolm Grant: Thank you very much, Simon.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:29.570
On the first point that you touched on, which
was Expo 2015, I just feel that this is a

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:33.560
remarkable act of engagement between the NHS
and so many of our stakeholders.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.850
There were 5,000 people through the door every
day, and a good discussion - because it was

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.380
in Manchester - around the devolution package
there.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.720
I just hope that in future years we can continue
to build on this.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:50.370
It is a very important part of the NHS not
just presenting what it is doing, but listening

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:55.870
to a much broader community who engage with
us in different events: a pop-up university,

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:00.180
different seminars over a concentrated two-day
period.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:06.199
So thanks to you, and also, of course, to
Tim Kelsey and his team, for actually preparing

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:12.791
such a fine programme - as you say, at no
cost to us or to the taxpayer.

00:05:12.791 --> 00:05:17.340
I invite any comments or questions to the
Chief Executive on that report.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.600
No?

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.340
Well, thank you very much, Simon.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:21.740
That is terrific.

